2. The 0/0 ambiguity

The general displayed energy formulas contain the formal lower-channel
quotients N/(N-1+delta) and N/(N-1+delta)^2. At the regular,
nondegenerate point N=0, delta=1, literal substitution would form 0/0.
Those terms represent the nonexistent state |-1> and must therefore be
removed before division, not simplified after an undefined quotient has
been created.

3. Final manuscript sentence

The first term in \eqref{eq:weak-drive-energy4} is absent for $N<2$; for
$N=0$, every lower-channel contribution proportional to $N$ is omitted
before division. Thus $e_0^{(2)}=-1/\delta$ and
$e_0^{(4)}=1/[\delta^3(1+2\delta)]$, giving $e_0^{(4)}=1/3$ at $\delta=1$.

The equation number is supplied by the existing LaTeX label
eq:weak-drive-energy4 and is not hard-coded in the source.

4. Independent symbolic check

The physical Rayleigh–Schrodinger recurrence in scripts/11a_verify_weak_drive.py
was evaluated from N=0 with its state loop bounded below by n=0. Consequently
no coefficient or denominator for a negative-number state was ever formed.
SymPy returned

  e_0^(2) = -1/delta
  e_0^(4) = 1/[delta^3(2 delta + 1)]
  e_0^(2) + 1/delta = 0
  e_0^(4) - 1/[delta^3(1+2 delta)] = 0

At delta=1 it returned exactly

  e_0^(4) = 1/3.

This agrees with the lower-channel convention already documented in
docs/bender_bettencourt_weak_drive_resummation.md and implemented by the
stage-11a helper. The stage-11d test also exercises N=0, delta=1 explicitly.
No script, audit document, diagonal recurrence, or BB core result required a
change, and no second-subdiagonal summation was started.

